{{Quote|She bundled these things and more together not in an old, dead rancor hide, but swaddled in the living fronds of giant ferns that grew beside the Misty Falls.|Falta recounting her story to Bug|<ref name="Bug" />}}
The '''Misty Falls''' were a group of waterfalls on the [[planet]] [[Dathomir]]. During the [[Republic Era]], the [[Dathomirian]] [[witch]] [[Falta]] visited the Misty Falls. She used the giant [[Fern (plant)|fern]]s near the falls to bundle a group of items in a [[burial pod]] which would create her daughter [[Yenna]], in a process contrary to the [[burial]] customs of the [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] clan.<ref name="Bug" /> Sometime between [[20 BBY]] and [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date">"[[Bug (short story)|Bug]]" is set during the [[Clone Wars]] and several [[Standard month|months]] after the [[Battle of Dathomir]]. ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the battle to [[20 BBY]], and the end of the Clone Wars to [[19 BBY]]. Thus, the short story must take place between those two [[Standard year|years]].</ref> Falta traveled to an [[Unidentified inn (Sídi)|inn]] on the [[planetoid]] [[Sídi]] where she recounted her excursion to the [[Youngling|young]] girl known as "[[Bug (Sídi)|Bug]]."<ref name="Bug" />

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Misty Falls were mentioned in the [[2020]] short story "[[Bug (short story)|Bug]]," written by [[E. Anne Convery]] and published in ''[[The Clone Wars: Stories of Light and Dark]]'' anthology.<ref name="Bug" /> In the ''[[Star Wars Legends]]'' continuity, the [[Misty Falls/Legends|Misty Falls]] first appeared in the [[2003]] [[Sony]] Online Entertainment [[Star Wars video games|video game]], ''[[Star Wars Galaxies]]''.<ref name="SWG">{{SWGcite|exp=AED|type=location|Misty Falls|Dathomir}}</ref>

